# Button

Triggers an action, or renders an anchor when given an `href`. Styled with theme tokens and shadcn variant names.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
</script>

<Button>Button</Button>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/button.json
```

## Variants

Set `variant` to `default`, `secondary`, `outline`, `ghost`, `destructive`, `link`, or `bare`. The default is `default`, and `bare` drops the background, border, and padding so the content is the whole button.

<Demo section="variants" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Button>Default</Button>
<Button variant="secondary">Secondary</Button>
<Button variant="outline">Outline</Button>
<Button variant="ghost">Ghost</Button>
<Button variant="destructive">Destructive</Button>
<Button variant="link">Link</Button>
<Button variant="bare">Bare</Button>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Button size="xs">Size xs</Button>
<Button size="sm">Size sm</Button>
<Button size="md">Size md</Button>
<Button size="lg">Size lg</Button>
```

## Icons

Place an icon before or after the text and the padding tightens to fit. For icon-only buttons, use the square sizes `icon-xs`, `icon-sm`, `icon-md`, and `icon-lg`, and add an `aria-label`. With `variant="bare"`, the square shrinks 8 pixels below the control height and the icon fills it with no padding, so `icon-xs`, `icon-sm`, `icon-md`, and `icon-lg` show 16, 24, 28, and 32 pixel icons for inline actions such as copy or close. Bare buttons take the surrounding text color, dim on hover, and show a thin `--ring` outline instead of the focus ring.

<Demo section="icons" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
	import { ArrowRightIcon, MailIcon, PlusIcon, XIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Button><MailIcon />Login with email</Button>
<Button variant="outline">Continue<ArrowRightIcon /></Button>
<Button size="icon-md" variant="outline" aria-label="Add"><PlusIcon /></Button>
<Button size="icon-sm" variant="bare" aria-label="Close"><XIcon /></Button>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius from the size.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Button variant="secondary" rounded="sm">Rounded sm</Button>
<Button variant="secondary" rounded="pill">Rounded pill</Button>
<Button size="icon-md" rounded="pill" aria-label="Add"><PlusIcon /></Button>
```

## Links

Pass `href` to render an anchor with the same styles. A disabled link drops its `href`, sets `aria-disabled`, and leaves the tab order.

<Demo section="links" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Button href="/docs/components">Browse components</Button>
<Button href="/docs/components" variant="link">Text link</Button>
<Button href="/docs/components" variant="outline" disabled>Disabled link</Button>
```

## States

Set `disabled` to dim the button and block clicks. Set `aria-invalid="true"` to show the invalid ring, such as for a form submit that failed validation.

<Demo section="states" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Button disabled>Disabled</Button>
<Button variant="outline" aria-invalid="true">Invalid</Button>
```

## API

The `Button` props extend the native `button` attributes, or the `a` attributes when `href` is set. Extra attributes and event handlers such as `onclick` pass through to the element.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface ButtonBaseProps {
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
	/** Visual style of the button; `bare` drops the background, border, and padding, and its icon fills an `icon-*` size */
	variant?: "default" | "outline" | "secondary" | "destructive" | "ghost" | "link" | "bare";
	/** Size on the shared scale, or a square `icon-*` size for icon-only buttons */
	size?: UiSize | `icon-${UiSize}`;
}
```
